L0285: Unsupported stored reference type

The reference or lifetime spelling is outside the supported shared-reference model. Stored mutable references are not implemented; lend &mut for a checked call instead. State named lifetimes for supported stored shared references and preserve their source ownership.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/reference_in_let.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// Stored shared references require a borrow expression rather than a bare
// referent value. Mutable references still last for one call.
struct Holder {
    inner: &u8,
}

fn longest(a: &u8, b: &u8) -> &u8 {
    a
}

fn kept(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let r: &u8 = n;
    n
}

fn nested(n: &&mut u8) -> u8 {
    n
}

fn rebound(mut n: &mut u8) -> u8 {
    n
}
```

Language, as built: [1.26:4](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.26:4).
